    "content": "# Study Roadmap 🗺️\r\n\r\nThis roadmap outlines structured study plans for mastering system design across three timeline options: **4 Weeks (Interview Sprint)**, **8 Weeks (Comprehensive Track)**, and **12 Weeks (Staff+ Mastery Track)**.\r\n\r\nTrack your progress by checking the boxes as you complete each topic.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## ⚡ 4-Week Track: Interview Sprint\r\n\r\nDesigned for engineers with upcoming technical interviews who need high-yield preparation.\r\n\r\n### Week 1: Fundamentals, Estimation & Networking\r\n- [ ] [01. Fundamentals: Requirements, Scalability & Metrics](docs/01-fundamentals/01-what-is-system-design-and-requirements.md)\r\n- [ ] [01. Fundamentals: Availability Nines & SPOF](docs/01-fundamentals/04-availability-reliability-durability.md)\r\n- [ ] [20. Estimation: Numbers Every Engineer Should Know](docs/20-estimation-and-interview-framework/01-numbers-every-engineer-should-know.md)\r\n- [ ] [20. Estimation: Back-of-the-Envelope Math Guide](docs/20-estimation-and-interview-framework/02-back-of-the-envelope-estimation-guide.md)\r\n- [ ] [20. Framework: The 6-Step Interview Framework](docs/20-estimation-and-interview-framework/03-the-6-step-interview-framework.md)\r\n- [ ] [02. Networking: TCP vs UDP & HTTP Evolution](docs/02-networking/03-tcp-vs-udp-and-congestion-control.md)\r\n- [ ] [02. Networking: DNS & CDN Edge Caching](docs/02-networking/02-ip-and-dns.md)\r\n\r\n### Week 2: Storage, Caching & Partitioning\r\n- [ ] [03. Load Balancing: L4 vs L7 & Algorithms](docs/03-load-balancing-and-proxies/01-l4-vs-l7-load-balancing.md)\r\n- [ ] [04. Caching: Strategies (Cache-Aside, Write-Through)](docs/04-caching/03-caching-strategies.md)\r\n- [ ] [04. Caching: Cache Invalidation & Pathologies](docs/04-caching/05-cache-invalidation-and-anomalies.md)\r\n- [ ] [05. Databases: SQL vs NoSQL Decision Matrix](docs/05-databases/05-sql-vs-nosql-decision-framework.md)\r\n- [ ] [05. Databases: Indexing Deep Dive](docs/05-databases/03-database-indexing-deep-dive.md)\r\n- [ ] [06. Partitioning: Sharding Strategies & Hotspots](docs/06-data-partitioning-and-replication/01-sharding-strategies.md)\r\n- [ ] [06. Partitioning: Consistent Hashing](docs/06-data-partitioning-and-replication/02-consistent-hashing.md)\r\n\r\n### Week 3: Distributed Systems & Messaging\r\n- [ ] [07. Distributed Theory: CAP Theorem & PACELC](docs/07-distributed-systems-theory/01-cap-theorem-and-pacelc.md)\r\n- [ ] [07. Distributed Theory: Consistency Models](docs/07-distributed-systems-theory/02-consistency-models.md)\r\n- [ ] [08. Messaging: Queues vs Pub/Sub vs Kafka](docs/08-messaging-and-streaming/01-message-queues-vs-pubsub-vs-streaming.md)\r\n- [ ] [08. Messaging: Outbox Pattern & CDC](docs/08-messaging-and-streaming/08-outbox-pattern-and-cdc.md)\r\n- [ ] [09. API Design: REST, Pagination & Idempotency](docs/09-api-design/01-rest-principles-and-resource-modeling.md)\r\n- [ ] [11. Reliability: Circuit Breakers & Retries with Jitter](docs/11-reliability-and-resilience/01-timeouts-retries-and-jitter.md)\r\n\r\n### Week 4: Essential Case Studies\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 01: URL Shortener (Deep Dive)](docs/19-case-studies/01-url-shortener.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 03: Distributed Rate Limiter](docs/19-case-studies/03-rate-limiter.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 04: Unique ID Generator](docs/19-case-studies/04-unique-id-generator.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 08: Real-Time Chat App](docs/19-case-studies/08-chat-messaging-app.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 09: News Feed Timeline](docs/19-case-studies/09-news-feed-timeline.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 13: Ride-Hailing (Uber)](docs/19-case-studies/13-ride-hailing-service.md)\r\n- [ ] [19. Case Study 17: Payment System (Idempotency & Ledger)](docs/19-case-studies/17-payment-system.md)\r\n- [ ] [20. Interview Prep: Mock Interview Evaluation Rubric](docs/20-estimation-and-interview-framework/06-mock-interview-evaluation-rubric.md)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🚀 8-Week Track: Comprehensive Engineering Track\r\n\r\nIdeal for engineers who want deep conceptual confidence and broad architecture coverage.\r\n\r\n- **Weeks 1-2**: All topics in [01. Fundamentals](docs/01-fundamentals/), [02. Networking](docs/02-networking/), and [20. Estimation](docs/20-estimation-and-interview-framework/).\r\n- **Weeks 3-4**: [03. Load Balancing](docs/03-load-balancing-and-proxies/), [04. Caching](docs/04-caching/), [05. Databases](docs/05-databases/), and [06. Data Partitioning](docs/06-data-partitioning-and-replication/).\r\n- **Weeks 5-6**: [07. Distributed Systems Theory](docs/07-distributed-systems-theory/), [08. Messaging & Streaming](docs/08-messaging-and-streaming/), [09. API Design](docs/09-api-design/), and [10. Architecture Patterns](docs/10-architecture-patterns/).\r\n- **Weeks 7-8**: [11. Reliability](docs/11-reliability-and-resilience/), [12. Security](docs/12-security/), [13. Observability](docs/13-observability/), and Case Studies 01 through 20.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🏛️ 12-Week Track: Staff+ Mastery Track\r\n\r\nComprehensive masterclass including low-level object-oriented design, machine learning pipelines, and all 35 case studies.\r\n\r\n- **Weeks 1-4**: Comprehensive distributed systems foundation (Sections 01 to 08).\r\n- **Weeks 5-7**: Cloud infrastructure, Security, Observability, and Storage (Sections 09 to 15).\r\n- **Weeks 8-9**: Real-time systems (Section 16) and Low-Level Design (Section 17 - SOLID, GoF, and all 10+ worked OOP problems).\r\n- **Week 10**: Data and ML systems (Section 18 - Data Lakes, Iceberg, Feature Stores, RAG architectures).\r\n- **Weeks 11-12**: Case Studies 01 through 35, mock interview loops, and ADR creation.\r\n",
