    "content": "# Recommended System Design Literature & Canonical Papers 📚\r\n\r\nCurated collection of seminal research papers, engineering blogs, and definitive books that form the foundation of modern distributed systems.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📖 Canonical Books\r\n\r\n1. **Designing Data-Intensive Applications (DDIA)** by Martin Kleppmann\r\n   - *The undisputed bible of modern distributed systems, storage engines, and consensus.*\r\n2. **System Design Interview – An Insider's Guide (Vols 1 & 2)** by Alex Xu\r\n   - *Clear visual guides for standard interview case studies.*\r\n3. **Site Reliability Engineering (SRE)** by Betsy Beyer et al. (Google)\r\n   - *Practical operations, SLOs, error budgets, and incident postmortems.*\r\n4. **Building Microservices (2nd Edition)** by Sam Newman\r\n   - *Decomposition strategies, bounded contexts, and service communication.*\r\n5. **Database Internals** by Alex Petrov\r\n   - *Deep dive into B-Trees, LSM-Trees, distributed storage, and consensus.*\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📄 Seminal Research Papers\r\n\r\n- **Google File System (GFS)** (Ghemawat et al., 2003) — Distributed storage across commodity hardware.\r\n- **MapReduce: Simplified Data Processing on Large Clusters** (Dean & Ghemawat, 2004) — Parallel batch processing.\r\n- **Bigtable: A Distributed Storage System for Structured Data** (Chang et al., 2006) — Wide-column storage.\r\n- **Dynamo: Amazon’s Highly Available Key-value Store** (DeCandia et al., 2007) — Consistent hashing, hinted handoff, and quorums.\r\n- **In Search of an Understandable Consensus Algorithm (Raft)** (Ongaro & Ousterhout, 2014) — Understandable consensus.\r\n- **Spanner: Google’s Globally-Distributed Database** (Corbett et al., 2012) — External consistency with TrueTime atomic clocks.\r\n- **Kafka: a Distributed Messaging System for Log Processing** (Kreps et al., 2011) — Distributed append-only commit log.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🌐 Top Production Engineering Blogs\r\n\r\n- [Netflix Technology Blog](https://netflixtechblog.com/)\r\n- [Uber Engineering Blog](https://www.uber.com/blog/engineering/)\r\n- [Meta Engineering (Facebook)](https://engineering.fb.com/)\r\n- [Stripe Engineering](https://stripe.com/blog/engineering)\r\n- [Discord Engineering](https://discord.com/category/engineering)\r\n- [Slack Engineering](https://slack.engineering/)\r\n- [GitHub Engineering](https://github.blog/category/engineering/)\r\n",
